sections.grading:
Grading is generally fine for me. In my semester, we have 3 major grading parts: case study, reading response, and debate(with a self review afterwards). The debate weighs the most than every thing else. Also note that, for these 3, your grades will be a weighted combination of the grades from the teaching team and from your anonymous peers. Apart from these, you get grades from several quizzes, attendance, and a short presentation.
My grades:
full attendance, almost full in all quizzes combined;
slightly higer than the LQ for the presentation and debate;
around the HQ for the reading response;
highest for the case study.
Final grade: B+
A little lower than I expected but acceptible after all.
